   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]dup[/I5]() function provides an alternative interface to the service provided by [A6][I7]fcntl[/I7]()[/A6] using the F_DUPFD command. The call [I8]dup[/I8]([I9]fildes[/I9]) shall be equivalent\nto:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A6": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I10]dup2[/I10]() function shall cause the file descriptor [I11]fildes2[/I11] to refer to the same open file description as the file\ndescriptor [I12]fildes[/I12] and to share any locks, and shall return [I13]fildes2[/I13]. If [I14]fildes2[/I14] is already a valid open file\ndescriptor, it shall be closed first, unless [I15]fildes[/I15] is equal to [I16]fildes2[/I16] in which case [I17]dup2[/I17]() shall return\n[I18]fildes2[/I18] without closing it. If the close operation fails to close [I19]fildes2[/I19], [I20]dup2[/I20]() shall return -1 without\nchanging the open file description to which [I21]fildes2[/I21] refers. If [I22]fildes[/I22] is not a valid file descriptor, [I23]dup2[/I23]()\nshall return -1 and shall not close [I24]fildes2[/I24]. If [I25]fildes2[/I25] is less than 0 or greater than or equal to {OPEN_MAX},\n[I26]dup2[/I26]() shall return -1 with [I27]errno[/I27] set to [EBADF].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
