     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A72][/A72]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A72": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_116_07\" id=\"tag_17_116_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00043",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Implementations may use file descriptors that must be inherited into child processes for the child process to remain conforming,\nsuch as for message catalog or tracing purposes. Therefore, an application that calls [I73]dup2[/I73]() with an arbitrary integer for\n[I74]fildes2[/I74] risks non-conforming behavior, and [I75]dup2[/I75]() can only portably be used to overwrite file descriptor values that\nthe application has obtained through explicit actions, or for the three file descriptors corresponding to the standard file\nstreams. In order to avoid a race condition of leaking an unintended file descriptor into a child process or executed program, an\napplication should consider opening all file descriptors with the FD_CLOFORK or FD_CLOEXEC flag, or both flags, set unless the file\ndescriptor is intended to be inherited by child processes or executed programs, respectively.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I73": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I74": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I75": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00044",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A76][/A76]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A76": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_116_08\" id=\"tag_17_116_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00045",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I77]dup[/I77]() function is redundant. Its services are also provided by the [A78][I79]fcntl[/I79]()[/A78] function. It has been included in this volume of POSIX.1-2024 primarily for historical\nreasons, since many existing applications use it. On the other hand, the [I80]dup2[/I80]() function provides unique services, as no\nother interface is able to atomically replace an existing file descriptor.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I77": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A78": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I79": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I80": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00046",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I81]dup2[/I81]() function is not marked obsolescent because it presents a type-safe version of functionality provided in a\ntype-unsafe version by [A82][I83]fcntl[/I83]()[/A82]. It is used in the POSIX Ada binding.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I81": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A82": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I83": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00047",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I84]dup2[/I84]() function is not intended for use in critical regions as a synchronization mechanism.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I84": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00048",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "In the description of [EBADF], the case of [I85]fildes[/I85] being out of range is covered by the given case of [I86]fildes[/I86] not\nbeing valid. The descriptions for [I87]fildes[/I87] and [I88]fildes2[/I88] are different because the only kind of invalidity that is\nrelevant for [I89]fildes2[/I89] is whether it is out of range; that is, it does not matter whether [I90]fildes2[/I90] refers to an open\nfile when the [I91]dup2[/I91]() call is made.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I85": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I86": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I87": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I88": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I89": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I90": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I91": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00049",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I92]dup3[/I92]() function with the O_CLOEXEC and O_CLOFORK flags is necessary to avoid a data race in multi-threaded\napplications. Without O_CLOFORK, a file descriptor is leaked into a child process created by one thread in the window between\nanother thread creating a file descriptor with [I93]dup2[/I93]() and then using [A94][I95]fcntl[/I95]()[/A94] to\nset the FD_CLOFORK flag. Without O_CLOEXEC, a file descriptor intentionally inherited by child processes is similarly leaked into\nan executed program if FD_CLOEXEC is not set atomically. The safe counterpart for avoiding the same race with [I96]dup[/I96]() is the\nuse of the F_DUPFD_CLOFORK or F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC action of the [A97][I98]fcntl[/I98]()[/A97] function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I92": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I93": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A94": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I95": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I96": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A97": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/fcntl.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I98": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
